            "review_title": "Review at Country Houses Cafe",
            "review_text": "69bertie\nLincoln, United Kingdom12009 contributions\n0\nIf the atmosphere inside doesn't get you, the old cars outside will\nMar 2015 • Friends\nDriving by in daylight to our nearby hotel, I noticed quite a number of old cars and other memorabilia but really failed to notice that it was a cafe. And a large cafe inside too. We were just going for a beer and some cooling ice cream but some very nice looking chips passed by, so they ended up on the table too. If you want more, there is plenty on the menu to choose from. \n\nIt does get packed out though (this was over the Tet holidays) around 6pm and on. Nice views down below from up on the upper levels with the water feature running on through. The Vietnamese do know how to make a good scene. Go Vap district is close to Ho Chi Minh airport, so getting here would take about 30 mins from the centre of District 1. As to the old cars, most look like pre-Vietnam war veterans.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten December 31, 2015",
